# PCGen campaign file for System Reference Document 5.2, the 2024 D&D ruleset.
#
# The .lst files here are generated by the scripts in tools/. Regenerate them
# rather than hand-editing.

# The name PCGen shows in its source list. It carries the community's
# name for the 2024 revision as well as the document's own, because
# those are different words and a player looking for this set will
# search for the first: WotC never called it 5.5e, and everyone else
# does. SOURCELONG below stays exact -- it is the attribution the
# CC-BY notice rests on, and that has to name the actual work.
CAMPAIGN:D&D 2024 (5.5e) - SRD 5.2.1
KEY:5e - SRD 5.2
# The key names the 5.2 line, not the point release. It is what saved
# characters and _phb2024.pcc's PRECAMPAIGN refer to, so it stays put when a
# revision lands; SOURCELONG and SOURCEDATE say which revision this is.
GAMEMODE:5e
# The core ruleset of the 2024 line, not a supplement to anything. Which
# matters for one specific reason: PCGen's own SRD 5.1 guards itself with
# !PRECAMPAIGN:1,BOOKTYPE=Core Rules,[5e - System Reference Document] -- "no
# other Core Rules book" -- and declared a Supplement, this set never tripped
# that guard. Both were then loaded together, both define an ability named
# Default in CATEGORY:Internal along with duplicate classes, races and spells,
# and RANK decided in 5.1's favour: the whole proficiency engine here was
# discarded without a word. Declaring what this is makes 5.1 stand aside, and
# is also what lets anything else ask for BOOKTYPE=Core Rules and find it.
BOOKTYPE:Core Rules
TYPE:Wizards of the Coast.Core
GENRE:Fantasy
SETTING:Dungeons & Dragons
RANK:202505
SHOWINMENU:YES
STATUS:ALPHA

SOURCELONG:System Reference Document 5.2.1
SOURCESHORT:SRD521
SOURCEWEB:https://dnd.wizards.com/resources/systems-reference-document
SOURCEDATE:2025-05

PUBNAMELONG:Wizards of the Coast
PUBNAMESHORT:WotC
PUBNAMEWEB:http://www.wizards.com

ISLICENSED:YES
ISOGL:NO

# ISLICENSED:YES raises a licence popup when the source is loaded, and it
# was raising an empty one: the flag was set and no LICENSE line existed to
# fill it. For a CC-BY-4.0 dataset that popup is exactly where the
# attribution belongs -- the licence is satisfied by giving credit, and a
# notice nobody is shown is not credit. This is the attribution text
# Wizards prescribes for SRD 5.2.1, reproduced rather than paraphrased.
LICENSE:This work includes material from the System Reference Document 5.2.1 ("SRD 5.2.1") by Wizards of the Coast LLC, available at https://www.dndbeyond.com/srd. The SRD 5.2.1 is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, available at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.

COPYRIGHT:System Reference Document 5.2.1 Copyright 2025 Wizards of the Coast LLC, available at https://www.dndbeyond.com/srd. Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License, available at https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.

INFOTEXT:System Reference Document 5.2.1, the 2024 D&D ruleset, released by Wizards of the Coast under CC-BY-4.0.
INFOTEXT:Contains everything in the SRD: 339 spells, 12 classes and their subclasses, 353 magic items from 258 entries, 235 monsters and 96 animals with their 1291 traits and actions and 398 attacks, 38 weapons, 13 armours, 291 items of gear, 19 feats, 4 backgrounds, 9 species and 393 kits.
INFOTEXT:Also carries the foundation a 5e source must supply itself: ability scores, saving throws, sizes, alignments, 18 skills, 19 languages and the weapon proficiencies.
INFOTEXT:Weapons carry their 2024 mastery property as FACT:Mastery.
INFOTEXT:Feats are sorted into the 2024 categories: Origin, General, Fighting Style and Epic Boon.
INFOTEXT:Epic Boons, Grappler and Ability Score Improvement apply their ability score increase as a choice.
INFOTEXT:Backgrounds grant ability score increases and an Origin feat, as the 2024 rules require.
INFOTEXT:Only the +1/+1/+1 background ability distribution is modelled, not the +2/+1 split.
INFOTEXT:Species grant traits only. In the 2024 rules ability score increases come from the background.
INFOTEXT:Monsters and animals carry their statistics; their traits and actions are description text rather than mechanics.

# The foundation. PCGen's 5e game mode does not define what an ability score
# is, or a size, or a skill -- those are data, and a source that does not
# supply them loads with no stats at all. These come first because everything
# below refers to them.
DATACONTROL:srd52__datacontrols.lst
ALIGNMENT:srd52__align.lst
SAVE:srd52__saves.lst
STAT:srd52__stats.lst
SIZE:srd52__sizes.lst

# Ability categories must load before the abilities that belong to them, and
# the base categories before the categories built on top of them.
ABILITYCATEGORY:srd52_abilitycategories_base.lst
ABILITYCATEGORY:srd52_abilitycategories.lst
ABILITYCATEGORY:srd52_abilitycategories_background.lst
ABILITYCATEGORY:srd52_abilitycategories_class.lst
ABILITYCATEGORY:srd52_abilitycategories_species.lst

# What a proficiency is worth. Everything that grants one -- classes,
# backgrounds, the first-level template -- refers to these by name, so they
# load before all of it. Skills load first because the proficiency of a skill
# names it.
SKILL:srd52_skills.lst
ABILITY:srd52_abilities_proficiency.lst

# Feats load before backgrounds, which grant them by name.
ABILITY:srd52_feats.lst
ABILITY:srd52_abilities_feats.lst
ABILITY:srd52_backgrounds.lst

# Species traits load before the species that grant them.
ABILITY:srd52_abilities_species.lst
ABILITY:srd52_abilities_lineage.lst
# And a creature's traits and actions before the creature.
ABILITY:srd52_abilities_monster.lst
LANGUAGE:srd52_languages.lst
BIOSET:srd52_biosettings.lst
RACE:srd52_races.lst
RACE:srd52_races_unselected.lst
RACE:srd52_races_monster.lst
RACE:srd52_races_animal.lst

SPELL:srd52_spells.lst

# Class features load before the classes that grant them by name, and the
# first-level templates after the classes their PRECLASS names.
ABILITY:srd52_abilities_class.lst

# The weapon masteries, one per weapon. Nothing grants them by name: the five
# Weapon Mastery features raise a pool and these are what it is spent on, so
# their only tie to the rest is the PREPROFWITHWEAPON each one carries.
ABILITY:srd52_abilities_mastery.lst
CLASS:srd52_classes.lst
# The Hit Dice a creature's levels are in, one class per die size. A
# monster is a monster because it has them; without them a Troll is a
# species carrying a Troll's ability scores.
CLASS:srd52_classes_monster.lst
TEMPLATE:srd52_templates.lst

# Proficiencies before the equipment that names them.
WEAPONPROF:srd52_profs_weapon.lst
ARMORPROF:srd52_profs_armor.lst
SHIELDPROF:srd52_profs_shield.lst
EQUIPMENT:srd52_equip_weapons.lst
EQUIPMENT:srd52_equip_armor.lst
EQUIPMENT:srd52_equip_general.lst
EQUIPMENT:srd52_equip_magic.lst
# A creature's own attacks. Loaded before the races that AUTO:EQUIP them.
EQUIPMENT:srd52_equip_monster.lst

# Starting equipment, one kit per printed option. After the equipment,
# because a kit names the gear it packs.
KIT:srd52_kits.lst
# And what puts a creature's own attacks in its hands.
KIT:srd52_kits_monster.lst
# The magic weapons. They are enchantments applied to a weapon above, not
# weapons, because none of them is one weapon: a Flame Tongue is any melee
# weapon and a Berserker Axe is one of three axes.
EQUIPMOD:srd52_equip_mods.lst

# The SRD has no deities. PCGen still requires one to mean "none chosen".
DEITY:srd52_deities.lst
